  "notes": [
    "The 26 new fixture sources/configs/previews were audited. Only stretch-in, kinetic-warp, and stage require newly retrieved default assets. Twelve fixtures use the existing Geist CSS variable, with matching existing Geist v5 latin font bytes confirmed against Google Fonts. Remaining defaults use system font stacks and inline vector/canvas artwork.",
    "Stretch In must fetch the frozen Anton TTF unchanged, parse it with upstream opentype.js 2.0.0, and await load before deterministic capture. Its default fontUrl is the Anton sourceUrl above.",
    "Kinetic Warp catalog config defaults to Passion One, weight 700, with the recorded Google Fonts stylesheet URL. The bare component defaults to sans-serif with an empty fontUrl. Use catalog defaults for the reference; localize the stylesheet URL in both fixtures and wait for the requested face before rasterizing text.",
    "PassionOne.css preserves upstream declarations, weights 400/700/900, and latin/latin-ext ranges. Only URLs are made relative. Original response is preserved as PassionOne-upstream.css.",
    "StageExampleScene uses the exact committed WebP and contentSize 1265 by 10022. Replace staticFile with the frozen local asset path in installed HTML, without resizing or recropping.",
    "Ship each font with its copyright and OFL notice. Passion One has Reserved Font Name Passion. Font files were not altered. Retain Remocn MIT for its source and Stage example asset, and opentype.js MIT when its code is included.",
    "opentype.js 2.0.0 package matches the integrity pinned by Remocn bun.lock and declares no runtime dependencies. Existing Remocn runtime dependencies were outside this new-asset audit.",
    "The reused Geist font matches Google Fonts Geist v5 latin exactly. Its current Google Fonts OFL notice is frozen here as Geist-OFL.txt; the older existing assets/fonts/Geist-OFL.txt has a different copyright line and was not changed."
  ]
